          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കായികതാരം — kāyikatāraṁ — \"an athlete\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ കായികതാരം ഓട്ടത്തിൽ സ്വർണ്ണം നേടി. ā kāyikatāraṁ ōṭṭattil svarṇṇaṁ nēṭi. That athlete won gold in the race."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കായികം of the body, sport + താരം a star."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കായികതാരം (kāyikatāraṁ) is a learned compound built from Sanskrit kāyika, \"done with the body\" (Monier-Williams), and താരം, from Sanskrit tārā, \"a star\" (CDIAL 5798)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
